Feature: Controllers
  The CONTROLLERS screen lists the USB joysticks and gamepads that are plugged in, and what
  `controls.cfg` maps. SET UP CONTROLLER starts the sim on the plain T1-S, with the radio
  wizard. The wizard opens when the sim sees a controller. It saves `controls.cfg`. When the
  sim closes, the launcher reads `controls.cfg` again. RESCAN looks for the controllers again.

  Expectation: SET UP CONTROLLER starts the radio wizard on the T1-S Ranger
    When the pilot sets up the controller
    Then the program in the log is the radio wizard
    And the plane of the started sim is the T1-S Ranger

  Expectation: The launcher reads controls.cfg again when the wizard closes
    Given the controls file is missing
    And the program in the log is the radio wizard
    When the radio wizard saves controls.cfg and closes
    Then the controls file is mapped
